==Ukrainian==

===Etymology===
Created in {{etyl|orv|uk}} following {{term|азъбукы||tr=azъbuky|lang=orv|sc=Cyrl}}, borrowed from {{etyl|cu|uk}} {{term|азъбоукы|tr=azŭbuky|lang=cu|sc=Cyrs}}, formed from the names of the first two letters in the [[Cyrillic alphabet]], {{term|азъ||tr=azŭ|lang=cu|sc=Cyrs}} + {{term|боукы|tr=buky|lang=cu|sc=Cyrs}}, following the example of Greek {{term|ἀλφάβητος||lang=el|sc=Grek}}.

Attested 1627, compare {{term||язъбука|tr=jazъbuka|lang=uk|sc=Cyrl}} (17–18th century). 

===Noun===
{{infl|uk|noun|tr=ázbuka|g=f|sc=Cyrl}}

# {{dated}} [[alphabet|Alphabet]] (an ordered set of letters used in a language), especially the old [[Cyrillic]] alphabet.

====Synonyms====
* [[абетка]]
* [[абетло]] (''dialectic'')
* [[алфавіт]]
* [[альфабет]]

====Derived terms====
* [[азбучний]]
* [[азбучна війна]] (''proper noun'', ''historical'')

====Related terms====
* [[аз]]
* [[буква]]

